BT /F2 13 Tf 72 595 Td (1. Purpose) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 575 Td (This policy defines the governance framework for the complete lifecycle of AI models within) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 562 Td (MT&T Corporation, from development through deployment, monitoring, and retirement. It ensures) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 549 Td (all AI models meet quality, security, fairness, and compliance standards before and during) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 536 Td (production deployment.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 72 503 Td (2. Model Development Standards) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 483 Td (All AI models must be developed using MT&T-approved frameworks and registered in Unity) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 470 Td (Catalog's Model Registry. Each model must have a Model Card documenting: purpose and intended) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 457 Td (use cases, training data sources and lineage, performance metrics and evaluation results,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 444 Td (known limitations and biases, responsible AI assessment results.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 421 Td (Foundation models accessed via the Databricks Foundation Model API or AI Gateway must be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 408 Td (pre-approved by the AI Ethics Committee. Currently approved foundation models include: Meta) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 395 Td (Llama 3.3 70B, Anthropic Claude family, OpenAI GPT-4 family, Google Gemini family, and DBRX.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 382 Td (Provisioned throughput endpoints must be justified with a cost-benefit analysis showing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 369 Td (expected usage above 60% utilization.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 72 336 Td (3. Model Deployment Approval Process) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 316 Td (Before any model is deployed to a serving endpoint, it must pass through a three-stage) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 303 Td (approval gate: Stage 1 \(Technical Review\) - The MLOps team validates model performance,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 290 Td (resource requirements, and serving configuration. Stage 2 \(Security Review\) - The Security) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 277 Td (team verifies access controls, data classification compliance, and AI Gateway guardrail) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 264 Td (configuration. Stage 3 \(Business Review\) - The business owner confirms the model serves an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 251 Td (approved use case and budget allocation exists.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 228 Td (Emergency deployments may bypass Stage 3 with approval from two VP-level sponsors, but must) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 215 Td (complete full review within 5 business days post-deployment.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 72 182 Td (4. Production Monitoring Requirements) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 162 Td (All production model serving endpoints must be monitored using the AI Governance Dashboard.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 149 Td (The following metrics must be tracked: Request volume and trend via v_serving_endpoint_daily,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 136 Td (Token consumption and cost via v_ai_cost_daily, Error rates and latency via) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 123 Td (v_ai_gateway_daily, User access patterns via v_ai_access_audit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 100 Td (Model owners must configure alerts for: Error rate exceeding 5% over a 1-hour window, Latency) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 87 Td (exceeding SLA thresholds \(p99 < 2 seconds for chat, < 500ms for embeddings\), Cost exceeding) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 74 Td (120% of monthly budget allocation, Drift in input distribution detected via Databricks) Tj ET
endstream
